Why this licence is proposed
----------------------------
The package contains data derived from two third-party datasets and must not grant more than their terms allow.

* ACCIDENT (Kaggle `picekl/accident`). The Kaggle listing states CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The ACCIDENT paper states
  CC BY 4.0 for the annotations and metadata, Apache-2.0 for code and CARLA assets, and upstream terms for the
  videos. The two statements conflict; the stricter Kaggle terms (non-commercial, share-alike) are applied
  here until the dataset authors clarify. Some real clips originate from other Kaggle uploads with their own
  terms. The manifests (clip identifiers, anchors, class labels, splits, timing) and all stored answers,
  audit results and re-analysis outputs are derived from this dataset.
* MM-AU (Hugging Face `JeffreyChou/MM-AU`, revision 540cb1277cb70e91a7022abe852decb3ee9adb0a) is released
  under CC BY-NC 4.0. The MM-AU part of the package (ledgers, development manifest, predictions and
  evaluations) is derived from it; CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 satisfies its non-commercial and attribution terms.

Not covered: the package contains no raw videos, frames or pretrained weights. Obtain the datasets and models
from their sources under their own terms. Files that reproduce the authors' own protocol and pre-registration
(accident/protocol/, accident/prereg/) are also part of the code repository under its licence.

Open points for the authors: confirm the licence choice; confirm or obtain the ACCIDENT authors' position on
the licence conflict; decide whether the ShareAlike term is required for the MM-AU-only files.
